{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,pathlib\np=pathlib.Path('metadata.json')\ndata={\n'sourceInformation':{'date':'2026-11-05 20:15:37','source':'Pressure Cooker (1983), Activision; original arcade cooking reinterpretation. Specific source details beyond native model knowledge: unknown.','plan':'none','genre':'Arcade action; cooking and time management','perspective':'Fixed elevated three-quarter orthographic 3D','tech':'Three.js 0.180.0 / R180; WebGPURenderer with WebGPU and WebGL 2 fallback; Rapier 3D 0.19.3; Gamepad API; Web Audio API; AI Hub session client 1.4.0 / protocol v1; esbuild 0.25.12. All runtime dependencies embedded.','artDirection':'Procedural cel-shaded diner diorama, ink outlines, warm paper, terracotta and mint palette.','animation':'Three.js AnimationMixer and AnimationClip with authored breathing, walking, spatula flick, serve jump and customer idle tracks; procedural food and effect motion.','audio':'Code-generated swung diner jazz, synthesized effects and formant-like Animalese/Simlish-style gibberish. No audio files. Music defaults to 10%.','online':'AI Hub synchronized parallel score attack, 1–4 players; standalone solo and 1–2 player couch co-op. No standalone remote matchmaking.','testing':'Headless scripted logic and browser tests, whole-game AI playthrough, emulated standard gamepads, touch profiles, Web Audio levels, AI Hub conformance harness and visual screenshots. Physical controller, real touch hardware and listening: unknown.','research':'No internet search. Source design uses native model knowledge. Supplied AI Hub protocol/client/harness fetched directly; pinned npm dependencies downloaded.','environment':'Codex CLI (headless); Linux / Ubuntu 26.04 on WSL2','model':'OpenAI, gpt-6.1-sol, reasoning effort max','usage':'added on import'},\n 'testingFeedback':['unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown'],\n 'engineFeedback':['Three.js native toon materials, orthographic cameras and AnimationMixer made a consistent illustrated diorama straightforward.','unknown','The complete cooking simulation, order UX, controller navigation, touch assistance and procedural audio.','Coordinating fixed simulation steps, Rapier bodies, native animation and two rendering backends in a single-file build.','none','A first-party controller-first UI and input layer would reduce custom infrastructure.'],\n 'promptFeedback':['The source, art direction, input philosophy and deliverable were concrete enough to support a coherent complete game.','Whether standalone multiplayer needed remote networking in addition to AI Hub sessions; this implementation provides couch co-op outside the hub.','Combining a polished single-file WebGPU game with accessible controls, an entire three-rush progression and tested multiplayer integration.','Specify whether standalone remote multiplayer is mandatory, and distinguish direct dependency/protocol downloads from prohibited internet research.'],\n 'aiHub':{'name':'Pressure Griller','tagline':'A little lunch. A lot of hustle.','description':'Catch conveyor toppings, stack the regulars’ burgers and hustle to the right counter in an inked 3D diner. Beat three escalating lunch rushes solo, share a kitchen with a friend, or compete for tips in AI Hub.','type':'Game','genre':'Action','source':'Pressure Cooker (1983)','series':'','players':'1–4','controls':'Move: left stick / WASD. Catch or serve: Cross / Space. Dash: Circle / Shift. Bell: Triangle / Q. Ticket: R1 / Tab. Clear tray: Square / R. P2: arrows / Enter. Touch: drag, assisted catching.','tags':['3d','arcade','cooking','co-op','retro','comedy']}}\np.write_text(json.dumps(data,indent=2))\nPY\nnpm run build\nnode --input-type=module - <<'JS'\nimport {Kitchen,autopilot} from './core.js';\nconst g=new Kitchen();g.start();for(let i=0;i<40000 && g.phase\"'!=='\"'result';i++)g.update(1/60,g.players.map(p=>autopilot(g,p)));console.log(g.snapshot());\nJS\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
