{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_76","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"biome check --write --linter-enabled=false --assist-enabled=false core.js audio.js scene.js ui.js main.js build.mjs core-tests.mjs\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,datetime\np=Path('metadata.json');d=json.loads(p.read_text())\nd['sourceInformation']['audio']='Code-generated swung diner jazz, synthesized effects and pitched Animalese/Simlish-style gibberish. No audio files. Music defaults to 10%.'\nd['sourceInformation']['testing']='110/110 automated checks passed: cooking rules, complete three-rush campaign with native physics, keyboard/mouse, two emulated standard gamepads, touch, sampled Web Audio output, GPU-loss recovery, and AI Hub conformance (2 players; 4 players with 150 ms latency, 50 ms jitter and 5% loss; host departure). Layouts reviewed at 1920×1080 and 390×844 through WebGL 2; healthy WebGPU state checked directly because headless captures can be blank. Physical hardware and actual listening: unknown.'\nd['testingFeedback']=[\n '4 game/UX issues found during testing and review: graphics-loss recovery, live ticket-patience reset synchronization, title/mobile layout wrapping, and co-op collider spawn alignment. Test-driver fixes were tracked separately.',\n '1 potentially game-breaking issue: losing the WebGPU device could leave a blank kitchen. Automatic WebGL 2 recovery now preserves the game state and passed deliberate device-loss testing.',\n 'The scripted full three-rush playthrough with native Rapier physics, followed by the supplied AI Hub harness under four-player network impairment and host departure. The final suite passed 110/110 checks.',\n 'The first headless WebGPU screenshots. A blank capture could not distinguish a rendering failure from a screenshot limitation, so direct device-state checks and WebGL layout captures were needed.'\n]\nd['engineFeedback']=[\n 'Native toon materials, orthographic cameras, and AnimationMixer clips made the illustrated diner and expressive chef animation straightforward.',\n 'Yes. Initial software WebGPU canvas presentation destroyed the device, even in a bare-canvas probe. Adding --use-angle=swiftshader to the test browser resolved that environment issue; the game also gained graphics recovery.',\n 'The cooking/order simulation, controller-first UI and navigation, touch assistance, input translation, procedural audio, and session lifecycle.',\n 'Coordinating fixed-step Rapier movement, native animation, WebGPU/WebGL recovery, and portable single-file packaging while preserving game state.',\n 'none; Three.js and Rapier source are unchanged. Rendering recovery uses an application callback.',\n 'A first-party controller-first UI and input layer, including focus navigation and standard gamepad glyphs.'\n]\nd['promptFeedback']=[\n 'The concrete source, art direction, control philosophy, attract-mode requirement and single-file deliverable supported a coherent complete arcade game.',\n 'Whether standalone multiplayer required remote networking as well as AI Hub integration. This game supplies couch co-op outside the hub and synchronized online score attack inside it.',\n 'Combining a complete three-rush game, procedural visuals and sound, every input method, live dev tools and verified session integration in a portable HTML file.',\n 'Clarify whether standalone remote multiplayer is mandatory, and explicitly distinguish direct protocol/dependency downloads from prohibited internet research.'\n]\np.write_text(json.dumps(d,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nr=Path('test-run-process.json');v=json.loads(r.read_text());v.update({'completed':datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat(),'result':'110/110 checks passed; 0 failures.','running':False});r.write_text(json.dumps(v,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\nnpm run build --silent\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,re\nroot=Path.cwd().parent;stem=Path.cwd().name\nmeta=json.loads(Path('metadata.json').read_text());interview=json.loads((root/'exit-interview.json').read_text());html=(root/(stem+'.html')).read_text()\nassert meta==interview\nassert set(meta)=={'sourceInformation','testingFeedback','engineFeedback','promptFeedback','aiHub'}\nassert [len(meta[k]) for k in ['testingFeedback','engineFeedback','promptFeedback']]==[4,6,4]\nassert all(isinstance(v,str) and v.strip() for v in meta['sourceInformation'].values())\nassert meta['sourceInformation']['usage']=='added on import'\nassert 'CREDITS_DATA' not in html and 'THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES' not in html and '<\"'!-- GAME_SCRIPT -->'\"' not in html\nembedded=json.loads(re.search(r'<script id=\\\"credits-data\\\" type=\\\"application/json\\\">(.*?)</script>',html,re.S).group(1))\nassert embedded==meta\nassert Path('hub/session.js').read_text() in html\nassert 'Copyright © 2010-2025 three.js authors' in html\nassert json.loads(Path('test-results.json').read_text())['failed']==0\nprint('Final package verified: embedded credits match exit-interview.json; all 110 recorded checks passed.')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
